  "source_review": [
    "The new patch changes the GNU C Library LANGUAGE-entry check, preserving the reviewed upstream v7 guard and regression bytes. Existing strfmon and resolver fixes remain. The stable Makefile context is rebased; there are no application endpoint, authentication, authorization, cryptography, SQL or subprocess changes.",
    "The native regression reproduces four traversal failures before the fix. The patched library must pass the same upstream test, including normal translation and valid-entry fallback, with an explicit PASS assertion rather than an unsupported/skip outcome. Runtime package checks require glibc +trip2; the distribution assessment requires its actual ELF fingerprints and retains raw findings.",
    "Every previously bound query and supporting file has the identical LF-normalized SHA256. All fresh blocking results are compared individually by query, source region, original severity and semantic flow. Unknown identities, changed source or changed flows abort this review rather than refreshing them automatically."
  ],
